WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:30.876 --> 00:00:35.856
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.710
WILLIAM R.: I'm
coming from a family--

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:32.835
seven children, three sisters,
four brothers, and my parents.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.580
We were living an average
life, a very religious life.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:43.810
My father, he was
an Orthodox Jew.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.810
And I went to Haida.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:49.890
I went to Polish school.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:53.720
And I learned a trade.

00:01:56.648 --> 00:01:58.440
MALKA B.: What I remember
from my childhood

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:03.000
was a small family,
not very wealthy.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.015
We all lived in--

00:02:05.015 --> 00:02:08.970
in a neighborhood which
later was the ghetto.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.610
My father was a printer,
had a printer shop,

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:14.100
and worked there with a helper.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.590
My mother was a housewife.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:16.830
We were two children.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.180
We used to walk to
school quite a long time.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.570
It took an hour
perhaps, and on foot.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:25.380
We met, children together,
so we did not walk alone,

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.230
and, um, talked.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.300
And we were excited and
studied poetry on the way.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.680
So it was sort of nice.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.370
LEON G.: We had nine children.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:42.600
We had, you know, five
brothers and four sisters.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.380
We are, right now,
already at three--

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:48.090
two brothers and one sister.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:52.380
We had also two nephews and
a grandfather in our house.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:57.090
And we remain only three
of us from all of them,

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.180
all of them when.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:04.500
Living in Czestochowa, we
had a shop from tailoring.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.120
My father was a tailor.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:12.120
We all children worked in
the shop, in the tailoring.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:16.080
We had a wonderful time as kids.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.960
We are-- there we played.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.660
We belonged to a
Zionist organization.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.490
We played ping pong,
football, anything.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:26.250
What we had was
a wonderful time.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:33.060
WILLIAM R.: I personally
live a social, a good life--

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.120
I would say, the average life--

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:43.190
because, in my time, that
time, I had a good trade.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:44.370
And I was mating--

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:50.620
making family.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:58.800
So, at that time, if you
had enough to feed yourself

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:08.585
and to buy for yourself nice
clothes and, once a week,

00:04:08.585 --> 00:04:13.550
if you was able to go to a
movie with your girlfriend,

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.460
that was a luxury.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:18.292
LEON G.: I person
who ask of, uh, you

00:04:18.292 --> 00:04:20.959
know, a kid over there something
like that-- how come, you know,

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:23.030
you don't play this and that?

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:24.770
Well, he said you were Jewish.

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:26.210
I said, what's the difference?

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.132
So he said, you killed Christ.

00:04:29.132 --> 00:04:30.590
I said, what do
the-- oh, uh, well,

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.630
how-- and I didn't understand,
you know, what they are--

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:33.380
you know.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.227
He said, you killed Christ.

00:04:35.227 --> 00:04:36.310
I said, I didn't kill him.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.000
What do you want from me?

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.980
He said, you killed him.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.695
So that was a very-- the--
the religion, you know,

00:04:42.695 --> 00:04:45.950
was, uh, got, uh, a lot of
thing to do in-- in the school.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:48.200
In the city, we had three
miles away from-- from where

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.740
we lived over there, we had
the holy shrine over there.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.180
WILLIAM R.: In Czestochowa--

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:57.270
in Polish, you say Czestochowa,
that was the biggest church.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.740
Whoever you talked to--

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.970
and if-- then he going to
tell you the same thing,

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:08.630
that Czestochowa was the
biggest anti-Semitic city.

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:10.295
LEON S.: I make so much money.

00:05:10.295 --> 00:05:12.170
You know, I was
working two shifts.

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:16.130
And I was both shifts
in the-- in the factory.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:17.515
And I was working.

00:05:17.515 --> 00:05:20.120
And then I had two children.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:24.650
And really I had a bitter
life, beside money.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:27.500
I mean, money was
not questioned.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:31.280
It's like, uh-- so
this bitter life

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.020
was this was one
child was retarded.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:38.822
LUDWIG F.: In 1933,
we had been married.

00:05:38.822 --> 00:05:47.758
And we had a child
in 1937, a girl.

00:05:47.758 --> 00:05:51.730
And, uh, I was a very
successful businessman.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:54.460
PAULA K.: My father
knew his politics.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:56.650
He was all his life in this.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:59.680
So I heard then that I
was a child from 19--

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.560
I was born in 1924.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:05.020
But, in 1928, I was a little
child, five years, six years.

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:08.860
I always hear whole nights
he used to stay at the radio

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:10.065
and hear all his speeches.

00:06:10.065 --> 00:06:12.490
At that time, I didn't
understood who's-- who was

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:13.380
speaking, you know.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:16.090
But, later, I found out.

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:18.460
He knew it is going
to be something.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.250
LEON G.: Oh, we didn't, uh, we
didn't understand too much, you

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:22.720
know, what's going on, you see.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:23.368
We didn't know.

00:06:23.368 --> 00:06:25.660
And, even, they said, you
know, Hitler is in Palestine.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:26.730
You're going to go to Palestine.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:27.710
You're going to get--

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:29.290
Hitler is coming, or
something like that.

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:30.040
You killed Christ.

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:33.080
We didn't, uh-- you know,
we didn't know nothing.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.850
As, you know-- I didn't
know it was, uh, you know,

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:37.380
was going to be so bad.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:39.550
See, we wasn't organized.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:41.010
See, nobody told
nothing, you know.

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:42.820
Even, when you-- even
when you want to go away,

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:44.237
the father didn't
want to let you.

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:46.840
You didn't want to leave
your father and mother.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.440
You stood with the
family all together now.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.460
We wasn't trained to have a gun.

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:53.292
We wasn't trained
to have a knife.

00:06:53.292 --> 00:06:55.500
We wasn't trained to know
about this kind of business

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:56.200
over there.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.880
You know, stay away from us.

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:58.630
Stay away.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:06:59.530
You stay away.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:00.160
Stay away.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:02.440
We didn't-- we wasn't
nothing, you know.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.540
We just worked and
all, went to school.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:07.210
And we went to
the Polish school.

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:08.360
We went to Hebrew school.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:12.070
And, uh, and we go home
and work, uh, in the house.

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:22.450
PAULA K.: Well, I
was in the street,

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:26.000
and one day, bombs coming down.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:31.270
So everybody start to go back
to their houses and running.

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:35.360
It was already that time
a lot of people killed.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:39.230
And we hide it, so
didn't took too long.

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:44.510
MALKA B.: In '39 when Germans
took off over Czestochowa,

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:50.750
after very, very short fight,
during that time, we ran--

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:55.820
my family and I, I remember
hiding in a cellar.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:59.030
Probably when they
bombarded the city.

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:01.360
And hiding from the Germans.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:04.790
LEON G.: From Czestochowa to
the border, from German border,

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:07.420
was only 25 miles.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.850
You know, we was only,
not too far away from,

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:10.940
from them over there.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:15.902
That's why they was, in
1939, they started Friday.

00:08:15.902 --> 00:08:18.110
And Sunday, 10 o'clock, they
was already in the city.

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:19.610
It could be they
was there at night.

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:21.810
I didn't see it, because
at night I was sleeping.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:25.668
But that day, Saturday, I walked
out, and I see them fighting.

00:08:25.668 --> 00:08:27.710
And Sunday morning, when
I walked out over there,

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:30.880
it was 10 o'clock,
I took a walk.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:32.679
Three miles up to the
city hall over there,

00:08:32.679 --> 00:08:35.340
it was three miles from my house
to the city hall over there,

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:36.530
I took a walk over there.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:40.255
We see the German was already
all over, occupied the city.

00:08:40.255 --> 00:08:43.940
There was a friend of my father,
and I walked out over there,

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:44.780
went in over there.

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:47.380
His son was a friend
of mine over there.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.890
You know, we, I know that.

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:49.790
Also tailor.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:51.500
His name was Mr. Blitz.

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:56.220
And he said to me, now it's
time to kill ourself, that man.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:09:00.350
And I looked at him, I didn't
know what he was talking about.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:04.108
And I went up to the city
hall, and I went away--

00:09:04.108 --> 00:09:06.400
I ask this son if he want to
go for a walk, he said no.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:07.820
So I went myself.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:09.230
I went up three
miles over there,

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:12.290
and saw the Germans and all,
the city hall, I wanted to see.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.870
They put the German flag up
and everything like that.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:15.860
I see the whole story.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:18.740
And after, when I walked
back, I walked back,

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.977
and in the evening, I
went again over there,

00:09:21.977 --> 00:09:23.060
and he was killed already.

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:23.935
INTERVIEWER: Who was?

00:09:23.935 --> 00:09:26.120
LEON G.: He throwed
him-- that Mr. Blitz.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:28.580
So he went up on
the third floor,

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.890
and he throw himself down,
and he killed himself.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:44.930
The next morning,
all the people,

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:47.700
they tell us with the bayonets
over there and everything.

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:51.470
We lost-- the Bloody Monday,
they call it Bloody Monday--

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:56.900
we lost at the Bloody
Monday, 300 to 400 people.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:59.898
They just raus, raus, out,
out, out, out, out, out,

00:09:59.898 --> 00:10:01.940
with a bayonet and
everything, out, out, and out.

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:03.860
And then they had
that, they, they, they

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:06.430
show you the way to go to
the, to the green over there.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.770
All the bayonet was open
with the guns and everything

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:09.830
like that.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.415
Just like that with
the bayonet, they

00:10:11.415 --> 00:10:13.040
was going and all
the thing over there.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:15.940
This was the Bloody Monday, they
started right in the morning.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:19.190
And this was our first
day, the first, I mean,

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:21.570
the first day of the
Bloody Monday over there.

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:23.810
LUDWIG F.: They ordered
the whole Jewish population

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:32.060
of that city to get to
certain points, gather,

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:35.060
and the death
happened, they picked

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:41.180
at random, just every so
one, and just shot him.

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:44.140
We were there, and
I was in a barracks

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:46.340
as there were quite a
few thousand people.

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:53.390
And then they just had
been released to go home.

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:59.850
And since then, we
know what to expect.

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:06.120
Every day, another branch
of the German troops

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:10.480
of Germans and Gestapo
of the City Hall

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:15.005
had been picking up people
in the street at random,

00:11:15.005 --> 00:11:18.490
whatever they could,
to do their work.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:21.200
LEON S.: The first of
all, they throw out

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:24.205
the Jews, the rich
Jews, from the houses,

00:11:24.205 --> 00:11:26.640
and they took away everything.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:32.770
They put us between three,
five families in a two,

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:36.070
in a two bedroom apartment.

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:38.440
So I saw it's very bad.

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:42.160
MALKA B.: My father's
printer's shop was closed.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:46.210
The Germans took
over the machinery.

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:49.180
My school was closed,
so our teachers

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:52.760
decided to continue
education in their homes.

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:54.910
So I remember, we
walked in small groups

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:58.720
to their homes for
further instructions.

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:00.940
Then slowly, one
teacher disappeared,

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:02.460
we didn't know where.

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:05.080
Our doctors disappeared,
we didn't know where.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:08.720
It was all hushed, maybe
because I was a child then,

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:10.840
but maybe also people
really didn't know.

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:13.210
It was very gradually done.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:16.510
There were rumors that they were
taken to another city to work,

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:20.950
or they were needed because
intelligentsia, as we call it,

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:26.020
intelligentsia were slowly
disappearing from the city.

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:31.180
Doctors, professors, teachers,
directors slowly disappeared.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.280
So they were the first to go.

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:40.160
After a while, we
did not study at all.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:43.750
LEON S.: But they go to
work, people to work.

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:48.130
Any kind of work, not work
what is productive, productive,

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:52.440
only you know, to keep
Jews hard working.

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:55.330
So I said, I am a mechanic.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:13:00.250
And I want to do, I can
do any kind of work.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:01.960
So they took me to work.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:04.200
What they gave me, I did.

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.860
I tried to do the best--

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:10.720
I mean, the best as a mechanic,
not the best for them--

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:13.930
as a mechanic, to
show to be needed.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:17.740
To can keep there, for the
children, for the house.

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:32.450
WILLIAM R.: So they create the
ghetto, six or seven months

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:34.820
later, when they came
into Czestochowa. 'Cause

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:38.980
this was only 30 or 40 miles
from the German border.

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:51.810
Then we start to feel how
difficult it is to get food,

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:53.010
to get the first aid.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:14:02.017
And a Jew was not allowed
to leave the ghetto.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:10.460
We had some rationing
from the Jewish, they,

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:15.060
they create a Jewish
administration.

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:22.890
And I would say, used to
get 900 or 1,000 calories

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:23.880
for each head.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:26.220
That was in the beginning.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:28.640
Later was even not,
less than that.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:47.871
And between, young
people had to go,

00:14:47.871 --> 00:14:51.075
and to work for the Germans.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:59.670
The Jewish administration
used to point out

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.500
who has to go to work.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:05.410
LOLA J.: We had no
money to live on,

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:08.320
'cause jobs were not available.

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:10.560
So we struggle.

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:15.620
I used to go out of my,
I mean, out of ghetto,

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:22.590
I took off my armband,
and asking my,

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:25.270
my father's friend for help.

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:30.240
This the only way we
survived, just you know,

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.660
just whatever we could.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:33.690
It was very hard.

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:35.910
Begging people, please help me.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:40.460
We did have some nice people
who my father, rest in peace,

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.870
used to help them too.

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:45.900
And they gave me, you know, I
was carrying on my shoulder,

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.280
we'll call it the book sack.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:50.590
It's not, it's, what do
you call that, in the back,

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:51.503
you carry stuff.

00:15:51.503 --> 00:15:52.420
INTERVIEWER: Backpack?

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:53.550
LOLA J.: Backpack.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.965
And I was, had potatoes.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:15.290
Following day, after Yom
Kippur, they surrounded us,

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:18.340
and put us on a big market.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:21.610
Left and right,
young ones, even two.

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:24.740
We're just plain lucky
that we got in on the side.

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:30.011
My sister and my
mother were separated.

00:16:30.011 --> 00:16:31.850
from the
{?_{?_[NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]._?}._?}

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:33.120
And I was screaming.

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:35.870
And I said, mama, I was crying.

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:40.460
And one of the who surrounded
us was a Jewish guy who helped,

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:42.200
who had to be helped.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:47.660
And he said, you be happy,
because you're going to work.

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:49.020
And he shut me up.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:53.330
I say like, somebody says,
your life is going to be saved.

00:16:53.330 --> 00:17:00.140
And I said, mama,
and I screamed.

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:02.100
So he shut me up.

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:03.050
He said, don't scream.

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:12.430
So I was separated from
my sisters, two sisters.

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:14.343
And then this was the end.

00:17:14.343 --> 00:17:15.760
MALKA B.: Before
we knew it, there

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.839
was a very harsh
knock on the door.

00:17:17.839 --> 00:17:19.720
The door burst open.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:23.670
Assessment came in, with rifles,
out, out, out, out, in German.

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:26.780
And we were forced out.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:30.730
When-- I never saw my
home anymore after that.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:36.208
We were taken out into the
street, very fast, very loud.

00:17:36.208 --> 00:17:38.500
I probably was shocked, I
didn't know what's happening.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:41.590
But still I had my mother,
my father, another girl,

00:17:41.590 --> 00:17:45.750
young girl who lived with
us, who helped my mother also

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:46.630
was taken.

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:50.860
And they arranged us quickly
with rifles in fives, and five,

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:51.790
and five, and five.

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:54.070
And all my neighbors
were coming out

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:58.060
of their houses and apartments.

00:17:58.060 --> 00:18:01.120
And fives, and fives, and
fives were arranged that way,

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:02.830
and marched forward.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:04.750
And we came to a
certain spot where

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:07.180
the Germans separated people.

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:09.910
And because the five people were
always members of the family,

00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:11.535
they knew exactly
what they were doing.

00:18:11.535 --> 00:18:13.240
They separated the families.

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:15.400
So for us, my mother
was separated.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:20.980
Of course, with a gun pointing
to left, right, left, right.

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:23.440
My mother and the girl
who worked with her

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:24.700
were to one side.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:27.970
My father and my brother
and I, to the other side.

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:31.480
At that point my father
wanted to run to my mother,

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:32.740
to go with her.

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:34.870
Well, they hit him
with a gun, and not

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:36.620
killed him, just set
him, pushed him away,

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:39.640
and he went back to us.

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:40.600
Mother disappeared.

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:42.715
I didn't know then
where she went.

00:18:42.715 --> 00:18:44.840
Later I found out that this
was the first transport

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:46.840
to Treblinka.

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:48.020
So she was lost to us.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:50.020
We did not know where she went.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.080
My father and I and my brothers
remained together for a while.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:55.360
The Germans sent my
brother and my father

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.150
to work on a railroad track.

00:18:58.150 --> 00:19:00.340
They sent us to
work somewhere else.

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:03.010
Every day we returned
to the same place

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:05.290
were they stationed us.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:09.280
And one day, my father and
brother did not return.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:11.800
Again, I didn't know at that
time what happened to them.

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:15.520
Later I found out from witnesses
that they were both shot

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:18.623
on the railroad in the back.

00:19:18.623 --> 00:19:19.790
At that time, I didn't know.

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:22.900
But from that moment
when I was left alone

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:24.970
with other Jews who
were left alone,

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.680
without any links
to their family,

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:30.110
and I was barely 15 there.

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:34.660
LUDWIG F.: Every day, a
certain part of the city

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:39.700
has to be gathered in
a certain place where

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:43.150
they have decided which one
has to go right and left.

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:45.570
Which mean dead or to be alive.

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:01.680
MALKA B.: It was HASAG, Hugo
Schneider Aktiengesellschaft,

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:02.820
it was called.

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:05.120
It was a labor camp
in Czestochowa,

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:07.980
somewhere on the
outskirts of the city.

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:10.740
And what we did was, we--

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:15.780
they were bringing shells
from anti-aircraft guns,

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.310
or ammunition.

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:20.040
And the shells that were
destroyed, or partially

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:23.880
destroyed, or bent were
restored in that factory.

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:29.220
LUDWIG F.: Now I have
a wife and kid still

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:33.720
in the ghetto, which
hasn't been touched yet.

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:35.940
LEON S.: He knew I
have a sick child.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:39.060
He said, but us in
Germany, we are not

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:41.670
keeping people like this.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:48.180
We are giving the injection,
because the, the, the,

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:50.840
country has not a use
for such a people.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:54.450
If would be my son, I would
do the same, he advised me.

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:56.700
LEON G.: We went with Germans
that were inside in that

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:58.533
HASAG over there, and
we come in over there.

00:20:58.533 --> 00:21:01.260
The first thing, they lined
us up, all 300 people.

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:07.320
And we went up one flight.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:11.520
There was one huge room
for the 300 people.

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:14.680
Was 300 people, 150
laying on one side,

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:17.250
and 150, the other side.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.580
Was only one bathroom there.

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:21.515
And that's the
way we was inside,

00:21:21.515 --> 00:21:26.730
and this was the first
day without our parents.

00:21:26.730 --> 00:21:32.010
The first cry out that night,
we was choking me and crying.

00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:36.330
MALKA B.: I was 15, and I was
one of the youngest in camp.

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:38.270
All younger children
were killed and murdered.

00:21:40.475 --> 00:21:41.850
LUDWIG F.: You
have to understand

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:46.235
one thing, that
children two years old,

00:21:46.235 --> 00:21:50.040
overnight became 1,000 year old.

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:54.870
They know like rats,
that they will be killed.

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:56.370
LEON S.: I told
you, the first child

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:59.000
was, I have the sick child.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:02.380
When they liquidate the
ghetto, they took a truck.

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:05.280
And with the truck, they took
people with the children.

00:22:05.280 --> 00:22:09.360
Before I came in to
the, my apartment,

00:22:09.360 --> 00:22:12.500
the policeman told
me, was he a truck.

00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:14.850
And they took, a man went up--

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:17.610
I mean, from the children, Jews.

00:22:17.610 --> 00:22:22.290
They went up, and bought
a sleeping child down.

00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:25.830
And this was the
end from this child.

00:22:25.830 --> 00:22:31.240
LUDWIG F.: They start
to build a small ghetto

00:22:31.240 --> 00:22:36.050
from all these people who
were left in the factory.

00:22:36.050 --> 00:22:39.255
In order to do that,
they have picked women.

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:45.720
And they marched with
them to that small place

00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:49.910
where Jewish people used
to live, and to clean up.

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:57.060
And they were going about 10
{?_{?_[NON-ENGLISH SPEECH],_?},_?}

00:22:57.060 --> 00:23:02.790
the women, with pails and
everything which is needed

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:05.430
to clean up, brushes.

00:23:05.430 --> 00:23:11.220
My wife took the child, and
put in one of these pails.

00:23:11.220 --> 00:23:15.600
And go in, visit 10
{?_{?_[NON-ENGLISH SPEECH],_?},_?}

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:23.130
they went into that little
place where the ghetto will be.

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:27.850
Now going back, she hid
the kids under the bed,

00:23:27.850 --> 00:23:31.020
in that little
ghetto, overnight.

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:34.500
And the kid was by herself
until the next day,

00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:40.510
she came back again, and
gave her something to eat.

00:23:40.510 --> 00:23:42.660
This was for a few days.

00:23:42.660 --> 00:23:44.790
And in the end, they
took all of the rest

00:23:44.790 --> 00:23:46.800
and put in that ghetto.

00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:54.300
And all these people who were
sent to factories to work,

00:23:54.300 --> 00:23:57.360
had to go back everyday
into that new ghetto.

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:04.890
Now here again, we are
the whole family together.

00:24:04.890 --> 00:24:06.300
LEON G.: We had
one night we went

00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:13.820
home, was two guys who fell
asleep in, in the place.

00:24:13.820 --> 00:24:18.895
And we was counted to 298.

00:24:18.895 --> 00:24:22.200
And we took one guy
out, because every 50,

00:24:22.200 --> 00:24:24.225
they had the
responsible one guy.

00:24:24.225 --> 00:24:27.390
And they took out the guy,
you know, and they shot him.

00:24:27.390 --> 00:24:30.890
Because he didn't know
where the two guys was at.

00:24:30.890 --> 00:24:34.770
The next day, the two guys was
there, in the, in the factory.

00:24:34.770 --> 00:24:37.110
Nothing would happen
to them over there.

00:24:37.110 --> 00:24:40.910
I mean, it's, it was something,
you know, this everything

00:24:40.910 --> 00:24:42.290
what I saw it, you know.

00:24:42.290 --> 00:24:44.190
It was a young boy, the
same thing, you know.

00:24:44.190 --> 00:24:48.600
He was a cap maker, I know him
very good, I see him every day.

00:24:48.600 --> 00:24:52.370
I mean, I see him, in my,
my dream, I can see it.

00:24:52.370 --> 00:24:54.480
Because we all were together.

00:24:54.480 --> 00:24:56.410
LUDWIG F.: So
fortunate that we were

00:24:56.410 --> 00:25:01.168
working where the Pope
was, with the Holy Madonna,

00:25:01.168 --> 00:25:01.960
the Black Madonnas.

00:25:06.050 --> 00:25:10.100
And we got in touch, going
back and forth, you know,

00:25:10.100 --> 00:25:13.880
painting you just,
people go back and forth.

00:25:13.880 --> 00:25:16.190
With one of the sisters,
and we told them the story,

00:25:16.190 --> 00:25:22.290
we were just save our
kid, how to do it.

00:25:22.290 --> 00:25:29.150
And we gave them an address,
and a name of our former mate.

00:25:29.150 --> 00:25:33.080
Well, whatever they
arranged, that the maid will

00:25:33.080 --> 00:25:36.200
be at a certain
time, at that place,

00:25:36.200 --> 00:25:39.370
and the kid will just walk out.

00:25:39.370 --> 00:25:43.730
And so happened,
she took the child,

00:25:43.730 --> 00:25:47.540
and walked with the child
up to the post office.

00:25:47.540 --> 00:25:50.510
Over there was
another woman, they

00:25:50.510 --> 00:25:55.120
didn't know each other,
who took over the child.

00:25:55.120 --> 00:26:01.230
And that woman brought the
child into that monastery,

00:26:01.230 --> 00:26:04.460
through a closed door,
and she had to leave.

00:26:04.460 --> 00:26:06.890
There can be no witnesses.

00:26:06.890 --> 00:26:11.060
Then the door opened,
they took in the child.

00:26:11.060 --> 00:26:16.010
The child came in, they
have listed as a nun--

00:26:16.010 --> 00:26:19.900
an orphan of a Polish officer.

00:26:22.355 --> 00:26:27.170
LEON S.: The other child,
when I left the second place,

00:26:27.170 --> 00:26:31.070
I took away, so
I, so I be killed.

00:26:31.070 --> 00:26:34.100
Because they always were
joking, next day, next day,

00:26:34.100 --> 00:26:37.120
finish, you know.

00:26:37.120 --> 00:26:43.690
So I saw, and I had a connection
in the, from the underground,

00:26:43.690 --> 00:26:47.030
was an engineer,
electric in HASAG.

00:26:47.030 --> 00:26:51.020
He was living outside,
he was in underground.

00:26:51.020 --> 00:26:53.790
And he has the job as
electrical engineer

00:26:53.790 --> 00:26:56.600
in HASAG, in the
concentration camp

00:26:56.600 --> 00:26:59.160
where the metal factory was.

00:26:59.160 --> 00:27:05.420
You know, so I saw, maybe in
a day they will kept, keep me,

00:27:05.420 --> 00:27:08.620
and then they will
not let me out.

00:27:08.620 --> 00:27:13.190
So I have to, I have to give
the child, that person what I

00:27:13.190 --> 00:27:15.650
can have a connection with him.

00:27:15.650 --> 00:27:21.020
So I asked him, I give
you so much, so much money

00:27:21.020 --> 00:27:25.010
to keep my child with
your child, you know.

00:27:25.010 --> 00:27:27.240
And he agreed.

00:27:27.240 --> 00:27:30.270
And I trust him, because
he was in the underground.

00:27:30.270 --> 00:27:32.930
MALKA B.: We were extremely
hungry all the time.

00:27:32.930 --> 00:27:37.370
We were getting a piece of
bread maybe that big, dry bread

00:27:37.370 --> 00:27:38.340
for the whole day.

00:27:38.340 --> 00:27:41.382
So some of us could
resist and take

00:27:41.382 --> 00:27:43.090
a little bit in the
morning, a little bit

00:27:43.090 --> 00:27:44.930
at noontime, a little
bit in the evening.

00:27:44.930 --> 00:27:47.810
But most of us ate it
right away in the morning.

00:27:47.810 --> 00:27:51.475
And for lunch, we got some
potato peel soup, water

00:27:51.475 --> 00:27:53.420
and potato peels.

00:27:53.420 --> 00:27:56.240
For the evening, there were
some {?_{?_[NON-ENGLISH SPEECH],_?},_?}

00:27:56.240 --> 00:27:57.980
some coffee.

00:27:57.980 --> 00:28:02.570
And that was what, what
we lived on, three years.

00:28:02.570 --> 00:28:04.280
As far as I'm
concerned, I didn't even

00:28:04.280 --> 00:28:06.620
hope for being saved.

00:28:06.620 --> 00:28:09.080
We just knew that
someday we will die just

00:28:09.080 --> 00:28:10.330
like everybody else.

00:28:18.020 --> 00:28:22.140
PAULA K.: We looked out through
the windows, we saw, my God,

00:28:22.140 --> 00:28:24.000
fights.

00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:27.850
The Russian woman, they came,
they had a whole battalion.

00:28:27.850 --> 00:28:32.080
And they came and they fought
those Germans, and they were--

00:28:32.080 --> 00:28:34.400
I saw so much death again.

00:28:34.400 --> 00:28:36.940
MALKA B.: And all of a
sudden, a young Jewish man

00:28:36.940 --> 00:28:40.390
ran into the hall, opened the
doors, and told us, come out,

00:28:40.390 --> 00:28:42.130
come out, we are free.

00:28:42.130 --> 00:28:45.220
The Russians are here, the
Germans are running away.

00:28:45.220 --> 00:28:49.120
LOLA J.: Being in, in
camps, being in concentrate,

00:28:49.120 --> 00:28:52.510
we were just fighting
for every day.

00:28:52.510 --> 00:28:53.720
We never knew.

00:28:53.720 --> 00:28:56.350
There was expect
that any day it's

00:28:56.350 --> 00:28:58.750
going to happen, something.

00:28:58.750 --> 00:29:01.740
But after we were
liberated, we're

00:29:01.740 --> 00:29:05.080
sad, because where
we going to go?

00:29:05.080 --> 00:29:05.920
Where are you going?

00:29:05.920 --> 00:29:07.780
Nowhere is home.

00:29:07.780 --> 00:29:11.590
LUDWIG F.: I went
back to Czestochowa,

00:29:11.590 --> 00:29:15.670
and yes, I want to
pick up my child.

00:29:15.670 --> 00:29:17.820
I know she's in that monastery.

00:29:17.820 --> 00:29:19.880
But how are you
going to pick it up?

00:29:19.880 --> 00:29:21.000
She's there as an orphan.

00:29:23.690 --> 00:29:31.690
So my wife and I went there, and
we start talking to the nuns.

00:29:31.690 --> 00:29:34.160
She didn't believe it.

00:29:34.160 --> 00:29:35.620
She has no parents.

00:29:35.620 --> 00:29:37.900
She's a devoted kid
to Jesus Christ.

00:29:40.840 --> 00:29:45.430
The church, well, we just
couldn't let it go like that.

00:29:45.430 --> 00:29:50.290
We called in one monk,
and another monk.

00:29:50.290 --> 00:29:54.940
And then came the head man.

00:29:54.940 --> 00:29:59.460
And we tried to convince
them that this is our child.

00:30:02.080 --> 00:30:07.120
But then they came
up with a verdict.

00:30:07.120 --> 00:30:11.150
Let the child make
her own choice.

00:30:18.950 --> 00:30:23.350
She was walking from one end
to the other, back and forth.

00:30:23.350 --> 00:30:24.475
She didn't know what to do.

00:30:24.475 --> 00:30:29.790
And finally she
probably recognized me.

00:30:29.790 --> 00:30:34.730
And got to me, crying,
I want to go with you.

00:30:34.730 --> 00:30:39.580
LEON S.: So one day, there,
there, from the underground,

00:30:39.580 --> 00:30:45.710
the, the people stood there,
most people, you know,

00:30:45.710 --> 00:30:46.940
there's nothing.

00:30:46.940 --> 00:30:51.320
So they saw me in the
street, come with us,

00:30:51.320 --> 00:30:52.820
we're going to drink now.

00:30:52.820 --> 00:30:57.350
Say, a big, you know, a
party from the underground.

00:30:57.350 --> 00:30:58.700
I said, I can't go.

00:30:58.700 --> 00:31:00.860
I have to look for my child.

00:31:00.860 --> 00:31:03.710
And I can't trust no
more, for the underground,

00:31:03.710 --> 00:31:05.570
I don't know where is my child.

00:31:05.570 --> 00:31:10.280
So he, he told me, listen,
one, you have to know,

00:31:10.280 --> 00:31:12.170
go there and there.

00:31:12.170 --> 00:31:15.980
You will hear ever
thing what happened.

00:31:15.980 --> 00:31:22.310
And there is a lake,
and I went there.

00:31:22.310 --> 00:31:26.130
And I asked the neighbors
around, I knocked on the house.

00:31:26.130 --> 00:31:29.150
A woman told me, when
the Germans were here,

00:31:29.150 --> 00:31:32.670
somebody brought a child,
was crying, they was waiting.

00:31:32.670 --> 00:31:36.560
We went out on the lake
in the, in the morning,

00:31:36.560 --> 00:31:38.780
we found a dead child.

00:31:38.780 --> 00:31:41.660
Then we saw that,
we told the Germans.

00:31:41.660 --> 00:31:44.220
He said, that
child in the water.

00:31:44.220 --> 00:31:47.200
And I didn't want to
tell this my wife.

00:31:47.200 --> 00:31:49.250
What will help?

00:31:49.250 --> 00:31:50.450
I had this in me.

00:32:00.670 --> 00:32:02.410
MALKA B.: This is
me, and this is

00:32:02.410 --> 00:32:04.210
my friend who had that picture.

00:32:04.210 --> 00:32:07.100
She survived with her
father, from the same city.

00:32:07.100 --> 00:32:10.390
We were just neighbors,
and very close friends.

00:32:10.390 --> 00:32:13.180
And this Helen, and
I are only survivors.

00:32:13.180 --> 00:32:16.210
All these children,
these girls were killed,

00:32:16.210 --> 00:32:18.220
during the first Aktion.

00:32:18.220 --> 00:32:21.750
They were just, as they took
people out, five and five,

00:32:21.750 --> 00:32:25.180
they went, they went to death,
and we went to life, life.

00:32:28.100 --> 00:32:34.750
WILLIAM R.: We were a
family from 96 people.

00:32:34.750 --> 00:32:42.260
Uncles, aunts,
cousins, grandfathers,

00:32:42.260 --> 00:32:44.630
and I'm the only one
I'm still around.

00:32:48.230 --> 00:32:53.930
LUDWIG F.: People wonder why
we never smile, we never laugh.

00:32:53.930 --> 00:32:56.990
This part of our brain is dead.

00:32:56.990 --> 00:33:00.710
We don't know what is love.

00:33:00.710 --> 00:33:04.200
My child, my daughter
never laughs.

00:33:04.200 --> 00:33:06.590
She's now a grown,
wonderful person,

00:33:06.590 --> 00:33:09.392
she lives in Los
Angeles, California.

00:33:13.250 --> 00:33:20.480
And I have a son who lives in
Atlanta, Georgia who's married.

00:33:20.480 --> 00:33:22.750
He went through law school.

00:33:22.750 --> 00:33:26.060
So has my daughter.

00:33:26.060 --> 00:33:30.950
But the different between
that child's life and my son

00:33:30.950 --> 00:33:32.900
is in two worlds.

00:33:32.900 --> 00:33:35.870
It was just like coming
back from grave, dead,

00:33:35.870 --> 00:33:37.590
without feeling.

00:33:37.590 --> 00:33:42.460
Here people live normally,
playing the piano,

00:33:42.460 --> 00:33:46.130
having mates, good
times, they laugh.

00:33:46.130 --> 00:33:47.289
And here, we have death.

00:35:15.113 --> 00:35:19.856
[MUSIC PLAYING]

